        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gilbert Strang\n- Companies: MathWorks, dSPACE GmbH\n- Organizations: Massachusetts Institute of Technology\n- Products: Simulink, TargetLink\n- Topics: mathematical computing software, graphical programming environments, automatic code generation\n\nFacts:\n- Gilbert Strang is the MathWorks Professor of Mathematics at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology.\n- MathWorks is an American privately held corporation that specializes in mathematical computing software.\n- Simulink is developed by MathWorks as a graphical programming environment for modeling, simulating, and analyzing multidomain dynamic systems.\n- TargetLink is produced by dSPACE GmbH as software for automatic code generation based on a subset of Simulink and Stateflow models.",
